---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SectionHeader from "@/components/SectionHeader.astro";
import { withBase } from "@/lib/urls";
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Jihwan Park and his engineering notebook.">
  <section class="grid gap-10 border-b border-white/10 py-12 lg:grid-cols-[0.8fr_1.2fr] lg:py-16">
    <div>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-slate-500">About</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold text-white md:text-5xl">Jihwan Park</h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-slate-300 md:text-lg">I studied computer science and electronic engineering at Kyung Hee University, then started organizing my work around one practical question: how internal services and AI workloads behave when network access, storage recovery, GPU placement, memory, or hardware area are constrained.</p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-400">The public version of that work is intentionally sanitized. I write about constraints, architecture choices, recovery paths, and implementation details without exposing private infrastructure.</p>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3 text-sm text-slate-300">
        <a class="rounded border border-white/15 px-3 py-2 hover:border-signal hover:text-signal" href="https://github.com/Petooooo">GitHub</a>
        <a class="rounded border border-white/15 px-3 py-2 hover:border-signal hover:text-signal" href={withBase("/cv")}>CV</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="grid gap-5">
      <div class="rounded-md border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.03] p-5">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">Platform Work</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-300">Selected Docker-based services were moved toward a K3S-based internal platform, with private image distribution, service exposure, persistent storage, and deployment repeatability as the main concerns.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-md border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.03] p-5">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">Recovery Work</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-300">Longhorn-backed PVCs made the difference between stateless self-healing and storage-aware recovery visible: detach/attach time, rebuild behavior, service readiness, and realistic RTO/RPO boundaries.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-md border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.03] p-5">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">AI Systems Work</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-300">Graduation projects looked at AI workloads from the systems side: TFLM tensor memory reuse on constrained devices and bit-shift CNN acceleration on Zynq FPGA with area/runtime tradeoffs.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-12 lg:py-16">
    <SectionHeader eyebrow="Focus" title="What I Actually Track" description="The site is meant to preserve concrete engineering context rather than broad career slogans." />
    <div class="grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3">
      {[
        ["Dependency Paths", "Which container images, Maven artifacts, system images, and bootstrap services must be available when the external network or primary registry is not."],
        ["Recovery Timelines", "What has to happen between a node or storage failure and service readiness: pod scheduling, volume movement, replica rebuild, health checks, and operator action."],
        ["Execution Constraints", "How AI workloads change when the limiting factor is not only model accuracy but memory arena size, FPGA area, GPU allocation, dataflow, or degraded serving."]
      ].map(([title, body]) => (
        <div class="rounded-md border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.03] p-5">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">{title}</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-300">{body}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-white/10 py-12 lg:py-16">
    <SectionHeader eyebrow="Boundaries" title="What I Avoid Claiming" description="The strongest version of this site is specific and honest about scope." />
    <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
      {[
        ["Not A Generic Kubernetes Claim", "The point is not that I installed Kubernetes. The useful part is working through how a restricted-network Docker operation changes when image supply, storage, service exposure, and rollback paths are handled through K3S."],
        ["Not A Hot-Failover Claim", "Using Longhorn PVCs does not automatically mean zero downtime. I describe recovery as detach/attach, rebuild, readiness, and RTO/RPO behavior rather than overstating HA."],
        ["Not An AI Model Portfolio", "The AI thread here is operational and systems-oriented: full-GPU serving constraints, degraded availability, TinyML memory planning, and hardware-aware acceleration."],
        ["Not A Private Incident Log", "Operational details are generalized. The public artifact should show the engineering problem and tradeoff without exposing private hostnames, internal IPs, credentials, or raw logs."]
      ].map(([title, body]) => (
        <div class="border-b border-white/10 py-4">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white">{title}</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-300">{body}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
